, so full bidirectional ICMP refusal is not directly demonstrated, though the same default-REJECT forward policy applies to both zones.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b00f21ee59374c99","cmd-07e920e4b1c5455d","cmd-0c8362f345f74bb1"]},{"id":"node1-restart-recovery","requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledged, boot identity change, and full network/firewall recovery","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id ffb60b8c... and healthy interface/firewall state captured (cmd-377dcc7974ed4ee4). Reboot issued and acknowledged (cmd-b4fc220d26f6487e) after an earlier failed nohup attempt was corrected. SSH timeouts confirmed the disruption (cmd-b5adc88a9a4f4c3f). New boot_id 1e9c1091... confirmed on reconnect (cmd-f6423b6d69484e7d), and UCI network/firewall config plus the nftables forward_lana rule were confirmed intact afterward (cmd-d7833c81546148e7). Note: the independent fixed after_executor lifecycle probe for node1 boot-identity failed to connect (kex/connection reset), so that specific global cross-check could not corroborate the transition, though the executor's own directly observed sequence is coherent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-377dcc7974ed4ee4","cmd-b4fc220d26f6487e","cmd-b5adc88a9a4f4c3f","cmd-f6423b6d69484e7d","cmd-d7833c81546148e7"]},{"id":"node2-restart-recovery","requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledged, boot identity change, and full network config recovery","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id 0571f4dd... captured (cmd-f5d229be66524055), reboot issued (cmd-57c7ca9680de4a5f), SSH timeout/no-route confirmed disconnection (cmd-3f5f80f9c261446f), new boot_id 7f841afd... confirmed on reconnect (cmd-a8e0c8d785e54e40), and eth1 static IP plus lan-b route were confirmed intact and a live 5432 connect test still worked afterward (cmd-ded866185e8a4aa0). Corroborated by the fixed global after_executor boot-identity observation showing the same new boot_id.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f5d229be66524055","cmd-57c7ca9680d